    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0164" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/560.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The rebellion appears well organized and well directed. The whole of the new army
                    forces at Wuchang, about 15,000 men and comprising three army corps, have joined
                    the revolution, The rebellion is undoubtedly the most serious since the Taiping.
                    Thus far foreign interests have been carefully respected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
